          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Thomas Jefferson</strong><br>\nThomas Jefferson was born on April 13, 1743, in Shadwell, Virginia. He grew up in a wealthy family with six sisters and one brother. Jefferson was educated by private tutors and went on to study at the College of William &amp; Mary. He excelled in his studies, especially in philosophy and mathematics, and had a keen interest in classical languages.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Career Before Presidency</strong><br>\nBefore becoming president, Thomas Jefferson served in many government positions. He was the author of the Declaration of Independence in 1776 and served as the governor of Virginia during the American Revolution. After the war, he was a diplomat in France and the first Secretary of State under President George Washington.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Vice Presidency and Election as President</strong><br>\nJefferson became the Vice President in 1797 after losing to John Adams in the presidential race. However, in the 1800 election, he ran again and won, becoming the third President of the United States. His presidency was marked by efforts to expand the country's territory and limit the power of the federal government.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
